{
  "_doc": "The setup command of the superbased SDKs (sdk-api-surface.md section 17; SDK quickstart plan sections 3.5 to 3.8; lane L0). Python and TypeScript run these from 0.2.0 (sdk/python/tests, sdk/typescript/test); a planner is tested from plain facts, the network through stubs serving sdk/contract/fixtures/setup. Exit codes: 0 done, 1 unexpected, 2 waiting for a person, 3 refused, 4 environment, 5 sent but not seen in 60 s.",
  "since": "0.2.0",
  "sdks": [
    "python",
    "typescript"
  ],
  "exit_codes": {
    "0": "done: the hello arrived",
    "1": "unexpected error",
    "2": "waiting for a person: declined, expired, not clicked; a re-run continues",
    "3": "refused: plan, membership, no member keys, the month used",
    "4": "environment or usage: an unknown flag or two destination flags, no supported language, the package manager failed, self-hosted --org-url, rate limited",
    "5": "sent but not seen within 60 s"
  },
  "detection": {
    "_doc": "Phase 1 and the install command of phase 3 (sdk-api-surface.md section 17). A case's own sdks, when present, narrows the file's (the npm cases name typescript). Inputs: files (path relative to --dir -> content; a lock file's content is irrelevant, '' stands for it), installed (Python: distributions the project interpreter reports; null: none queried), setup_version. want: language (python, typescript, or null: none supported, exit 4), package_manager, targets (sorted, the target rows whose packages the project uses; auto: false targets listed too), install (argv; {python} is the project interpreter setup found; extras sorted; auto: false targets (openai-agents) are not installed), and for TypeScript esm and nextjs. Python package-manager table, first match: uv.lock -> uv add; poetry.lock or a [tool.poetry] table -> poetry add; pdm.lock -> pdm add; Pipfile -> pipenv install; else {python} -m pip install. TypeScript: pnpm-lock.yaml -> pnpm add; yarn.lock -> yarn add; bun.lock or bun.lockb -> bun add; else npm install. Python reads [project] dependencies, [tool.poetry.dependencies], requirements*.txt and Pipfile first, then installed; a requirement name is compared normalised (PEP 503). TypeScript reads dependencies and devDependencies of package.json. boto3 selects bedrock only when a .py file under --dir contains bedrock-runtime; @aws-sdk/client-bedrock-runtime selects it directly. The register entry's own dependencies come with @superbased/sdk, so an ESM install adds nothing.",
